reagent-name-medical-test-inotrope = experimental inotrope
reagent-name-medical-test-sedative = experimental anesthetic
reagent-desc-medical-test-sedative = Only affects experimental physiology. Causes unconsciousness at 4 bloodstream units. Progressively suppresses spontaneous breathing above 2 units; 10 or more stops it. Requires respiratory monitoring and assisted ventilation. Does not provide tissue repair or reverse brain death.
reagent-desc-medical-test-inotrope = Experimental cardiac stimulant. Only affects experimental physiology. Supports a weak existing heart at 2 to below 10 bloodstream units; 10 or more causes ventricular fibrillation. Does not repair tissue or revive an irreversibly damaged brain.
reagent-name-medical-test-analgesic = experimental non-sedating analgesic
reagent-desc-medical-test-analgesic = Only affects experimental physiology. Reduces perceived pain by 12 game points per bloodstream unit, up to 60 points at 5 units. Extra doses give no additional benefit. Does not heal tissue, stop bleeding, restore structural function or cause anesthesia.
